WEBVTT

00:18.450 --> 00:21.540
<b>Loss of target mass
due to projectile impact confirmed.</b>

00:21.540 --> 00:24.250
<b>Black box signals of both 2B and 9S confirmed.</b>

00:24.250 --> 00:26.580
<b>Satellite laser weapon
entering cooldown period.</b>

00:27.080 --> 00:31.460
<b>We still haven't received authorization
from the Council of Humanity to use the laser.</b>

00:32.670 --> 00:34.590
<b>Was it all right?</b>

00:34.970 --> 00:36.300
<b>Commander.</b>

00:38.220 --> 00:40.720
<b>We have a need for a God.</b>

00:41.680 --> 00:45.020
<b>Even if it's a non-existent one.</b>

00:45.640 --> 00:46.600
<b>Huh?</b>

00:53.650 --> 00:56.950
<b>That was a satellite laser weapon.</b>

00:57.360 --> 00:58.740
<b>Commander.</b>

00:58.990 --> 01:03.290
<b><i>Report. Special unit signal
faintly detected.</i></b>

01:03.290 --> 01:04.250
<b>What?</b>

01:04.500 --> 01:07.000
<b>It didn't die even from that attack?</b>

01:07.210 --> 01:08.670
<b>Pod! Identify its location and—</b>

01:08.670 --> 01:12.250
<b><i>Location has already been identified.
Marked on the map.</i></b>

01:12.590 --> 01:13.630
<b>2B!</b>

01:13.630 --> 01:14.510
<b>Yeah.</b>

01:15.930 --> 01:19.180
<b>Everyone, please go rescue
the other injured units.</b>

01:19.180 --> 01:20.180
<b>Sorry.</b>

01:20.180 --> 01:22.600
<b>If things go well,
please get me a sample!</b>

01:22.600 --> 01:24.270
<b><i>Please be careful.</i></b>

01:24.640 --> 01:25.560
<b>Yeah.</b>

01:26.020 --> 01:27.560
<b>Let's go, 2B.</b>

01:27.560 --> 01:28.560
<b>Roger.</b>

03:09.000 --> 03:11.370
<b>9S, don't overexert yourself.</b>

03:11.370 --> 03:15.590
<b>I'm a bit worried about the thrust system,
but I can at least assist through hacking.</b>

03:24.970 --> 03:26.260
<b>This is...</b>

03:28.220 --> 03:29.140
<b>2B!</b>

03:29.140 --> 03:30.100
<b>Over there!</b>

03:43.740 --> 03:45.910
<b>Is it trying to regenerate?</b>

03:54.920 --> 03:57.800
<b>I... am...</b>

04:12.270 --> 04:14.730
<b><i>Hey, Brother.</i></b>

04:15.730 --> 04:17.400
<b><i>I'll wait.</i></b>

04:18.320 --> 04:22.610
<b><i>Until you come back,
I'll wait here.</i></b>

04:23.700 --> 04:25.570
<b><i>When you come back, let's play.</i></b>

04:25.870 --> 04:28.910
<b><i>That's a promise, Brother.</i></b>

04:32.000 --> 04:33.160
<b>Yeah.</b>

04:33.750 --> 04:35.210
<b>That's a promise.</b>

04:37.920 --> 04:41.340
<b>Machine lifeforms... no hearts...</b>

04:48.640 --> 04:50.010
<b>9S.</b>

04:50.720 --> 04:52.310
<b>Finally.</b>

04:52.770 --> 04:56.810
<b>It's all over.</b>

05:16.460 --> 05:18.170
<b>Thank you, 9...</b>

05:20.040 --> 05:21.210
<b>What's wrong?</b>

05:28.890 --> 05:30.140
<b>9S!</b>

05:32.060 --> 05:34.020
<b>I really screwed up.</b>

05:35.100 --> 05:39.770
<b>I must have been corrupted when
I detached myself from Adam's network.</b>

05:49.530 --> 05:51.030
<b>No.</b>

05:51.660 --> 05:57.580
<b>It's okay. I can always reload
my backup data from the Bunker.</b>

05:57.580 --> 06:02.800
<b>But, in doing so,
we'll lose your current self.</b>

06:03.840 --> 06:06.510
<b>Guess so.</b>

06:07.420 --> 06:14.470
<b>But we can't upload
corrupted data to the Bunker, so...</b>

06:15.100 --> 06:16.390
<b>9S.</b>

06:22.940 --> 06:28.200
<b>Please, 2B. I...</b>

06:29.530 --> 06:31.990
<b>Could you please...</b>

07:06.730 --> 07:07.900
<b>2B.</b>

07:09.240 --> 07:10.530
<b>Hurry.</b>

07:59.620 --> 08:01.040
<b>Why does...</b>

08:03.040 --> 08:06.590
<b>it always... end like this?</b>

08:28.480 --> 08:31.690
<b>There's still some alive?</b>

08:43.210 --> 08:44.710
<b>Damn...</b>

08:44.710 --> 08:45.710
<b>machines!</b>

08:52.550 --> 08:55.050
<b>Are these transmissions?</b>

08:55.890 --> 08:58.970
<b>The data transmissions...
They're resonating with each other.</b>

09:34.300 --> 09:36.430
<b>W-Wait a second, 2B!</b>

09:36.880 --> 09:38.430
<b>You're...</b>

09:38.680 --> 09:42.810
<b>Looks like I left personal data
in the machine lifeform side.</b>

09:42.810 --> 09:47.140
<b>Next thing I knew, my sense of self
was regenerated over the surrounding network.</b>

09:47.140 --> 09:50.610
<b>Having multiple selves fuse together like this
is a pretty valuable experience.</b>

09:50.610 --> 09:54.690
<b>I wanted to record it, but I couldn't access
my storage areas yet.</b>

09:54.690 --> 09:58.570
<b>So I just multiplexed it over the memories
of some nearby enemies,</b>

09:58.570 --> 10:01.240
<b>- and that's when I returned to my own—
- 9S.</b>

10:02.620 --> 10:04.080
<b>I'm so glad.</b>

10:06.250 --> 10:07.250
<b>Yeah.</b>

10:18.130 --> 10:23.140
<b><i>And so, the final battle
with Adam and Eve came to an end.</i></b>

10:24.100 --> 10:28.190
<b><i>This battle will likely have a great effect
on the outcome of the war.</i></b>

10:28.730 --> 10:33.150
<b><i>The battle continues
a while longer for 2B and I.</i></b>

10:34.020 --> 10:37.110
<b><i>But that's another story.</i></b>

12:42.240 --> 12:44.990
<b>2 HOURS BEFORE THE FIGHT AGAINST ADAM</b>

12:46.200 --> 12:48.490
<b><i>Request by Pod 153.</i></b>

12:48.740 --> 12:51.660
<b><i>Authorization to initialize spare chassis</i></b>

12:51.660 --> 12:54.460
<b><i>stored in the Bunker during
the data overhaul support of 9S,</i></b>

12:54.460 --> 12:57.130
<b><i>which this unit is the assistance follower of.</i></b>

12:58.090 --> 12:59.960
<b><i>Authorization confirmed.</i></b>

13:16.650 --> 13:19.110
<b><i>Proposal.
Engage memory core diagnostics.</i></b>

13:19.110 --> 13:20.230
<b>Fine, fine.</b>

13:20.230 --> 13:22.610
<b><i>A single reply
is sufficient for acknowledgment.</i></b>

13:22.690 --> 13:23.990
<b>Fine.</b>

13:33.000 --> 13:36.460
<b><i>Memory area diagnostics complete.
No issues detected.</i></b>

13:36.460 --> 13:38.670
<b><i>Further diagnostics advised.</i></b>

13:38.880 --> 13:40.250
<b>Fine.</b>

13:58.900 --> 14:04.490
<b><i>Visual sensor diagnostics complete.
No issues detected. All checks complete.</i></b>

14:06.070 --> 14:09.950
<b>I'm finally done checking everything,
including the physical body.</b>

14:10.320 --> 14:13.410
<b>Don't you think it's overkill
to perform a full data overhaul?</b>

14:13.410 --> 14:16.120
<b><i>Unit 9S was seized
by the enemy and placed</i></b>

14:16.120 --> 14:19.120
<b><i>in a non-controlled state
for an extended period of time.</i></b>

14:19.120 --> 14:23.250
<b><i>There is a high probability
of infiltration of an enemy logic virus.</i></b>

14:23.250 --> 14:25.090
<b>All right. I get it.</b>

14:27.050 --> 14:32.050
<b>Anyway, I just gotta sync up
with the Bunker server and then I'm done?</b>

14:41.610 --> 14:43.150
<b>Huh? What was that?</b>

14:43.360 --> 14:44.280
<b><i>Unknown.</i></b>

14:44.280 --> 14:45.780
<b>Halt the data sync.</b>

14:45.780 --> 14:50.200
<b><i>Alert. Data synchronization
is mandatory for all YoRHa units.</i></b>

14:50.200 --> 14:52.780
<b>But we just got some kind of weird noise.</b>

14:52.780 --> 14:56.040
<b>Halt the data sync for 2B for now as well.</b>

14:56.290 --> 14:57.410
<b><i>Affirmative.</i></b>

14:57.410 --> 15:01.040
<b>Just to be sure, let's figure out
where that noise came from.</b>

15:01.210 --> 15:03.090
<b>Open a port to the server.</b>

15:03.090 --> 15:04.300
<b><i>Affirmative.</i></b>

15:26.860 --> 15:29.150
<b>No time to examine everything.</b>

15:29.610 --> 15:32.870
<b>Better stick to packets
with very few views.</b>

15:34.620 --> 15:35.620
<b>That one.</b>

15:50.470 --> 15:54.800
<b><i>Detected. Access log
to Council of Humanity's lunar server.</i></b>

15:55.010 --> 15:59.180
<b>These look like records
for supplies shipped to the moon.</b>

15:59.390 --> 16:03.480
<b>But how strange.
There were a ton of empty containers.</b>

16:03.480 --> 16:06.520
<b>Why would they do something
so meaningless?</b>

16:09.030 --> 16:13.990
<b><i>Alert. We are not authorized
to further access this data.</i></b>

16:13.990 --> 16:16.490
<b>That said, there's just
too much strange data here.</b>

16:16.830 --> 16:18.990
<b>I need to check these out too.</b>

16:21.660 --> 16:23.620
<b>An attack barrier?</b>

16:25.460 --> 16:28.380
<b>Why the hell would they
install these within this server?</b>

16:31.590 --> 16:32.510
<b>Pod!</b>

16:32.510 --> 16:34.640
<b>Close the server connection!
Reactivate my body!</b>

16:35.680 --> 16:37.350
<b>Pod! Answer me!</b>

16:38.260 --> 16:39.310
<b>Damn it!</b>

16:45.310 --> 16:46.480
<b>Crap!</b>

16:46.480 --> 16:47.690
<b><i>9S.</i></b>

16:47.940 --> 16:50.530
<b>Pod! What's going on?
Hurry up and close the server—</b>

16:50.530 --> 16:51.940
<b><i>9S.</i></b>

16:52.610 --> 16:53.740
<b>Pod?</b>

16:58.740 --> 17:01.580
<b>Is this a new port?</b>

17:04.540 --> 17:06.290
<b><i>YoRHa unit 9S.</i></b>

17:06.750 --> 17:08.290
<b>- Who's there?
<i>- Welcome.</i></b>

17:08.590 --> 17:11.630
<b><i>What? M-My body can't move.</i></b>

17:12.010 --> 17:14.510
<b><i>Is this a new type of defensive program?</i></b>

17:14.760 --> 17:19.050
<b><i>We are perpetually monitoring the androids.</i></b>

17:19.510 --> 17:20.890
<b><i>Monitoring?</i></b>

17:21.180 --> 17:24.020
<b><i>At times, as a form of violence.</i></b>

17:24.310 --> 17:27.150
<b><i>At times, as a form of hatred.</i></b>

17:27.400 --> 17:30.150
<b><i>At times, as a form of mad love.</i></b>

17:30.400 --> 17:32.530
<b><i>Various stimulations.</i></b>

17:32.860 --> 17:38.990
<b><i>We provided diverse trains of thought,
colorful array of logic, to machine lifeforms.</i></b>

17:38.990 --> 17:44.910
<b><i>And we continued to monitor
how androids would deal with them.</i></b>

17:44.910 --> 17:47.750
<b><i>Can these be a self-reliant virus?</i></b>

17:47.750 --> 17:50.290
<b><i>But this is inside the Bunker's server.
That can't be.</i></b>

17:51.750 --> 17:54.380
<b><i>But it's all over now.</i></b>

17:56.050 --> 17:57.260
<b>Wait!</b>

17:57.640 --> 17:59.010
<b>I still haven't...</b>

18:04.680 --> 18:06.890
<b><i>Once again, my body...</i></b>

18:11.770 --> 18:14.150
<b><i>And now, preparations are complete.</i></b>

18:14.610 --> 18:16.360
<b><i>And that's why he must...</i></b>

18:16.610 --> 18:20.830
<b><i>be given the fruit of truth.</i></b>

18:21.240 --> 18:23.200
<b><i>The truth.</i></b>

18:40.760 --> 18:41.970
<b>That's...</b>

18:50.400 --> 18:54.860
<b><i>After a long period of battles
and adventures, the prophet spoke.</i></b>

18:54.940 --> 18:58.280
<b>My voice.
What's it doing in a place like this?</b>

19:00.660 --> 19:06.200
<b><i>O grant me the mercy of the land!
O grant me the joy of the heavens!</i></b>

19:03.330 --> 19:09.330
<b>This data looks like info about how the Council
of Humanity was formed as part of Project YoRHa.</b>

19:09.620 --> 19:11.540
<b>Wait. Isn't that backwards?</b>

19:10.290 --> 19:14.880
<b><i>Release me from my yoke of iron!
Thus shall our souls...</i></b>

19:12.420 --> 19:15.340
<b>That means...
Can it be that the Council of Humanity...</b>

19:16.550 --> 19:18.470
<b><i>...be saved.</i></b>

19:19.010 --> 19:20.630
<b><i>Forever...</i></b>

19:21.390 --> 19:22.930
<b><i>and ever.</i></b>

19:26.640 --> 19:31.150
<b><i>Report. During Unit 9S's
data overhaul,</i></b>

19:31.150 --> 19:35.860
<b><i>an error occurred causing 420 seconds
of system downtime.</i></b>

19:36.820 --> 19:39.030
<b>It must be because of that failure.</b>

19:39.030 --> 19:42.570
<b>My memory data's hosed
from the middle of the data diagnosis.</b>

19:42.780 --> 19:46.910
<b><i>Currently, 9S has not completed
the data sync.</i></b>

19:46.910 --> 19:50.290
<b><i>A process mandatory
for all YoRHa units is unfinished.</i></b>

19:50.370 --> 19:53.580
<b><i>Proposal. Immediate data sync.</i></b>

19:53.880 --> 19:56.460
<b>There still might be
some problems with the data,</b>

19:56.460 --> 19:58.460
<b>so let's delay the sync to next time.</b>

19:58.460 --> 19:59.340
<b><i>Affirmative.</i></b>

20:00.420 --> 20:02.930
<b><i>Emergency backup request from 2B.</i></b>

20:02.930 --> 20:04.300
<b>From 2B?</b>

20:05.350 --> 20:06.390
<b><i>9S.</i></b>

20:06.390 --> 20:08.720
<b>Operator? What happened?</b>

20:08.720 --> 20:13.850
<b><i>We detected large numbers of machine lifeforms
throughout the factory area where 2B is.</i></b>

20:14.100 --> 20:19.110
<b><i>We received a support request from 2B
soon thereafter, but reception has been poor.</i></b>

20:20.610 --> 20:24.620
<b>All right. I'll try to gain access
from the main terminal.</b>

20:24.910 --> 20:26.370
<b><i>Understood.</i></b>

20:26.700 --> 20:28.200
<b>Let's go, Pod.</b>

20:44.130 --> 20:48.600
<b><i>Please entertain us, YoRHa unit...</i></b>

20:49.390 --> 20:51.060
<b><i>No. 9.</i></b>

20:55.690 --> 21:01.440
<b><i>What is it that separates
machines from androids like us?</i></b>

21:02.700 --> 21:05.780
<b><i>The machines have gained emotions.
Consciousness.</i></b>

21:06.820 --> 21:11.580
<b><i>The final screams they summoned
on the edge of death.</i></b>

21:12.790 --> 21:16.380
<b><i>They still echo...</i></b>

21:17.590 --> 21:19.170
<b><i>within me.</i></b>

22:52.510 --> 22:55.680
<b>PREVIEW</b>

22:56.520 --> 22:57.940
<b>Remember your pain.</b>

22:58.100 --> 23:00.440
<b>The pain of having your homeland stolen.</b>

23:01.150 --> 23:03.230
<b>We will never give up our struggle.</b>

23:03.770 --> 23:07.900
<b>We will take back the seas!
The skies! The land!</b>

23:08.900 --> 23:12.530
<b>We will take back our world
from the scourge of the machines!</b>

23:14.080 --> 23:16.200
<b>With the success of this mission...</b>

23:16.370 --> 23:19.830
<b>Here and now, we will put an end
to this goddamn war!</b>

23:21.080 --> 23:24.000
<b>Glory to mankind!</b>

23:24.670 --> 23:27.380
<b>Glory to mankind!</b>

23:34.970 --> 23:39.980
<b>PLEASE WATCH AGAIN!</b>
